# L §4.5: "known may be a window when the day is known only to lie in it ...; an as-known read on a day inside the
# window then states windows each or is HOLE-IMPRECISE (§4.4)."  The row of v2 is known within 2026-10-15..2026-11-01:
# as known 2026-10-20 it is imprecise; windows each splits at the day v2 becomes known: unseen (1) on any day of the
# window after the cut, seen (2) on a day by it (writer 8: windows earliest and latest are gone).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input n: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 1

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known window(2026-10-15, 2026-11-01)
  replace n = 2

ask q1: n as known 2026-10-20
ask q2: n as known 2026-10-20 windows each
ask q4: n
=== expect
q1: ?"date within window(2026-10-15, 2026-11-01) not precise enough for the cut 2026-10-20" ...
  cut 2026-10-20
q2 [known of v2 = 2026-10-15 .. 2026-10-20]: 2
  cut 2026-10-20
q2 [known of v2 = 2026-10-21 .. 2026-11-01]: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
q4: 2
  cut 2026-12-31
